X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Back of Beyond Books": "https://backofbeyondbooks.com/happenings/maggie-dewane-friday-may-23rd-630pm-grand-county-public-library/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:back_of_beyond
SUMMARY:Maggie Dewane
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260523T183000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260523T203000
UID:be51141663aaf7e24b2ee7c9b6730b8c@backofbeyondbooks.com
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, May 23rd @ 6:30pm\nGrand County Public Library\nJoin 
 author and poet Maggie Dewane for a nature-inspired poetry workshop. Magg
 ie will discuss the benefits of nature journaling and guide participants t
 hrough using haiku poetry as a tool of nature-based creative expression. B
 y the end of the workshop\, participants will have written their own haiku
  drawing inspiration from their favorite places. Maggie will also discuss 
 her book\,Haiku and Hope: 50 States of Climate Change\, an exploration of 
 the U.S. — places beloved and unfamiliar — and the changes to our home
 s we are likely to see\, as well as some of the good work being done to co
 mbat climate change.
LOCATION:Grand County Public Library\, 257 E Center St\, Moab\, UT 84532
URL:https://backofbeyondbooks.com/happenings/maggie-dewane-friday-may-23rd
 -630pm-grand-county-public-library/
X-SOURCE:Back of Beyond Books
END:VEVENT
